  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3501 (head d563eecb2). Work this issue after that PR merges.\n\n1. The test `each_shipped_rotary_post_declares_upright_after_tilt` (`crates/post/tests/upright_after_tilt.rs:272`) checks a fixed list of four posts (Fanuc, Doosan DNM, Mach4, Tormach). It does not read `assets/posts/*.cps`. A new post that accepts a tilted record and does not declare `uprightReturn` is found only at post time, by the refusal of the engine. That is the safe side, but a test that reads the folder finds it in the gate.\n2. The engine law reads the first motion record of a section: a `Move` or a `Cycle` (`crates/post/src/post/upright_after_tilt.rs:53-56`). Probe records (`Guard`, `Touch`, `Retreat`) do not count as motion. A probe section that opens with a guarded move after a tilted section is judged only from its first later `Move`. Check if the stream can give this case. If it can, count the probe records, and pin it.\n3. `crates/post/src/post/engine.rs` (640 lines) and `mod.rs` (735 lines) are over the 400-line limit. They were over it before PR #3501.\n",
